  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "It targets .NET Standard 2.0 and higher version. Supports double, float, Half and complex numbers. New in 2.1.0: on .NET 8 and higher, generic overloads of all real functions for any IEEE 754 floating-point type (float, Half and, on .NET 11 and higher, BFloat16, Decimal32, Decimal64, Decimal128); the float and Half overloads are kept and return the same results; fixed accuracy of generic complex Atanh and Acoth at Re z = ±1. On .NET 11 and higher, also supports generic Complex<T>. Since 2.0.0, complex functions return principal values with IEEE 754 / C99 branch-cut conventions, identical on all .NET versions.",
